WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.800
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.140
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.140
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.400
Hold this for me.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:36.990
What?

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.820
Is this a transmitter?

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:44.000
It's a cell phone. With this, we can quickly contact each other even if we're out.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.000
As long as you have a signal, that is.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.420
Don't get it wet though.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.460
Come on, let's get going!

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.800
How long are you expecting us to wait?

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.390
Sorry.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.890
What's the racket?

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:05.640
I've been telling you since yesterday. We're going shopping at Station Square.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:12.190
Since we now don't have to stay hidden inside the house, we should take full advantage of our freedom.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:17.490
Although it doesn't make any difference to Sonic because he does what he wants and went out.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.620
Sonic has a cell phone?

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.330
You can have it.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.120
Sonic, aren't you coming with us?

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.370
Have a good time.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.880
That's what I expected.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.010
Take me out on a date once in awhile! Sonic you meanie!

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.660
Episode 15

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.660
Raid of Egg Fort, the Flying Fortress!

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.230
Like I thought, Sonic doesn't like this kind of thing.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.360
He's not the type that always keeps in touch.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:01.490
He always disappears all of a sudden. I get worried when I can't contact him.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:07.540
Don't worry. He'll show up if something important happens.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.790
Really?

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.420
Definitely!

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.760
I found it!

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.470
I really wanted this.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.430
Chris...

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.690
Are we the center of attention?

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.360
I feel uncomfortable.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.490
Hey, is this real?

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.750
I'm sorry.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:39.880
He's the real deal! I saw him up close. What should I do?

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.510
You do something too!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.890
Tails, are you all right?

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.220
Hey...

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.140
What?

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.600
What's going on?

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.040
I'm scared.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.750
Are we that weird?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.750
You're the talk of the town because you're the heroes of the Eggman battle.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.170
But they're not treating us like heroes.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:27.840
Though I can understand if they're staring at me because of my beauty.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:32.680
I'm sorry. I never imagined it would turn out this way.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:36.230
I guess it can't be helped until everybody gets used to us.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.950
That's enough!

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.450
Let's go somewhere else.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.290
Please come this way.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.170
Amy, let's go.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.180
Wait!

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.180
Oh my, look at them.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:22.400
I heard the Thorndyke boy was living with strange creatures. I guess it's true.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.230
Please wait here for a moment.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.700
Only members can enter here, so we should be fine.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.990
I saw you on the news! You're so courageous!

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.170
You're so squishy!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:47.630
You said that we could relax here because it's members only.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:52.300
Oh no! I forgot that people here are always bored.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.640
They're the most aggressive crowd yet!

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.560
I'm scared.

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.600
Do your ears move?

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.190
That's enough!

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.210
That's good!

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.750
Be careful!

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.380
More over here!

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.420
Move out of the way!

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.600
You take care of that.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.900
A door.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.210
It can't be...

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:38.080
What is this?

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:14.780
Don't think that you crushed my will because of that measly incident.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:25.870
Tremble before the power of Egg Fort, the greatest airborne fortress I've secretly built for this very day!

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:30.170
Why did you use the drill and break down the door?

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.300
What a waste.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:38.090
What are you talking about. If I attached a drill, then it's a waste if I don't use it.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:40.260
Oh really?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.430
It's just a lot of trouble.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:46.810
Never mind that and go! Our destination is Station Square!

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.280
Eggman is alive.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:00.280
What?

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.870
A huge warship is heading this way?

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.290
Mayor!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:18.130
I've had enough. I'm not going into town for awhile.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:22.760
I think everybody will calm down if we give them a little more time.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:25.850
What's up?

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.140
Isn't that…

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.120
What is that?

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:46.620
Can it be...

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.880
Foolish humans.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:59.840
How dare you destroy my fortress the other day!

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:08.140
It's payback time. I will destroy Station Square and build a giant fortress for the Eggman Empire!

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:28.330
When did Eggman have time to build a battleship?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.370
Only if Sonic was here…

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.790
There's our limousine!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.270
Now's our chance to escape!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.170
Sonic!

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:24.050
See? I told you he would come!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.640
You've arrived, Sonic.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.220
You mess around too much, Eggman.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:52.910
Sonic, take this!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:11.270
It always turns out the same.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.080
No way!

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.450
He couldn't reach it.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.210
We need the X-Tornado. Let's go home and get it.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.290
But how?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.340
Hi, Chris.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.300
Are you in trouble?

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.090
Uncle!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:53.220
I'll take you home at top speed. Hang on tight.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:22.590
E-43 can track targets better than a missile.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.130
They're not easy to elude.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:39.900
That impudent brat!

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:43.860
Dr. Eggman, E-43 is equipped with a self-destruct device.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.860
That's right!

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:14.810
What a dreadful sound. Impressive, Sonic.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.640
I can't hold on.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.940
How's this!

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:46.920
Uncle, you're driving too fast.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.460
I'm only getting started.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.200
Mr. Stewart!

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:22.710
Hi Chris. Are you all right?

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.170
Stewart?

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.590
I'm Chris's homeroom teacher, Mr. Stewart.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.000
I met you once before.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:34.510
Oh, back then. I forget things quickly, but I also remember things quickly.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.260
You're Chris's uncle. Your name is...

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.180
Call me the wild express of love!

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:43.770
This isn't the time for introductions.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.520
X-Tornado.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.230
Oh yeah.

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:48.690
Stop dawdling.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:49.480
Why me?

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:50.320
C'mon.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.530
I'm stepping on the gas!

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.830
Here they come again!

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:05.580
It's so cramped that I can't use the mirror.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.840
We're finished!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.480
Mr. Tanaka!

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.100
X-Tornado!

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.230
Sonic!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.530
X-Tornado!

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:42.740
Got it!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.300
Fire! Fire! Shoot them down!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:03.810
Sonic?

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:09.850
If we fight here, people in the city will be injured.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:13.400
Sonic, we have to lead Eggman towards the ocean.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.650
Okay, leave it to me.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.160
Damn!

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:29.250
I'll give you a spanking! Sucker!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.920
Sonic, how dare you make fun of me!

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:39.720
After him! Capture that arrogant hedgehog!

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:43.140
He's easily provoked.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.760
He's hopeless.

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:46.020
Yeah.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:57.780
Has the army arrived yet?

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.120
Here he comes.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.420
Prepare to fire.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:24.510
Fire!

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:34.770
Farewell Sonic!

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:44.740
The energy circuit has been hit. The power is not going to last.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:46.030
What do you mean?

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:49.620
We can only fly at full speed for a few minutes!

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.710
What? Oh no!

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.670
I won't miss this time!

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.710
Prepare to fire the main gun!

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:01.970
Engaging coolants! Checking electrical circuits!

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:05.600
The machine is normal. Starting firing process!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.970
Energy recharge countdown!

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.390
So hectic.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:13.650
Why are there only three of us on this huge ship?

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:15.560
Stop complaining!

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:21.190
So you can fly at full speed for a few minutes?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.200
I guess so.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:27.160
Okay, aim for the bridge at full speed.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.450
That's crazy.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.080
Let's take that chance.

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.000
Has the energy recharged yet?

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:39.250
Not yet.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:41.550
It's the X-Tornado!

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.270
What are they planning to do?

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.200
Everyone, hang on!

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.670
Fire the main gun!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:24.550
There's still not enough energy.

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:38.440
He's coming!

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:43.740
We lost control of the aircraft!

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:45.450
It's over!

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:49.780
Sonic, you'll pay for this!

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.930
You did it, Sonic!

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:15.730
Sonic, you're the best!

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:19.440
But that wasn't enough to make Eggman give up.

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:23.360
Even though his base was destroyed, he still managed to make that.

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:25.280
He probably still has more...

00:22:25.570 --> 00:22:30.990
Yeah. The battleground might become more widespread.

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:42.460
Where's Eggman?

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:54.510
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:54.510
<i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i>

00:22:54.510 --> 00:23:03.480
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:54.510 --> 00:23:03.480
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:12.370
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:12.370
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:21.960
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:21.960
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:30.930
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:30.930
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:41.100
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:41.100
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:49.860
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:49.860
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:59.040
<b>Hikaru michi no fuuin ga tokeru yo</b>

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:59.040
<i>The seal to the shining path will be broken.</i>

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:03.880
<b>Hateshinaku</b>

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:03.880
<i>Forever...</i>

00:24:30.230 --> 00:25:35.430
Aim for it! The Sunken Ship in the Southern Seas
